<crash-analysis>
The crash is a heap-buffer-overflow in `glslang::TSymbolTable::findFunctionNameList`. The `table` vector has a size of 1, but the code attempts to access `table[level]` where `level` is likely -1, causing a read before the beginning of the allocated buffer.

The loop in `findFunctionNameList` should be modified to check the value of `level` before accessing the `table` array.

A possible patch would be to change the loop from a `for` loop to a `while` loop that checks the condition at the beginning:

```cpp
void findFunctionNameList(const TString& name, TVector<const TFunction*>& list, bool& builtIn)
{
int level = currentLevel();
while (level >= 0) {
table[level]->findFunctionNameList(name, list);
--level;
}
}
```

This ensures that `table[level]` is only accessed when `level` is a valid index.
</crash-analysis>

